      "created_at": "2021-01-02T20:14:30Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-01-02T20:17:01Z",
      "body": "Push to talk already is implemented in the web interface, but not easily discovered (issue #8322). It does not seem to be implemented in the mobile version (issue #8324).\r\n\r\nBut what I am requesting here is something else than push to talk, because not every user is going to be able (or want to) use that, so I still need the ability to mass mute and then help individuals unmute themselves. It is also helpful to have a \"prompt the participant to unmute with an un-missable super-obvious request overlay\" feature in general because, I swear, I've lost count of how many times I've spent five minutes trying to get my non-technical users to find the damned unmute button at the bottom and click it. They really need something un-mistakeable that I can put \"right in their face\".",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
