      "created_at": "2021-01-03T16:42:15Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-01-03T16:42:37Z",
      "body": "Dear @nekohayo,\r\nwe all know that a Moderator is able to mute another participant. Maybe at the same UI location, a Moderator also should be able to unmute. But by the other hand, this is a privacy problem: Especially if your participant isn't able to unmute by self, he probably don't notice that he was pushed \"on air\"!\r\n\r\nBTW: Such an tech-illiterate participant may be unable to unmute because don't know about the \"common used\" **icons**. To my experience it's better to tell him \"Please press the [M] button on you key board!\". The same yield for [V]ideo, of course ...\r\n\r\n",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
