      "created_at": "2021-03-05T14:40:44Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-03-05T14:40:44Z",
      "body": "Actually, there is a different use case where moderator-enforced muting AND unmuting could be beneficial to users.\r\n\r\nAt least in Italy, jitsi-meet is beeing widely used by schools to guarantee distance learning to children during lockdowns. This often turns messy when children unmute themselves at the wrong time, or fail to do so, or even mute/kick other kids.\r\n\r\nIt would be extremely useful to give moderators the chance to center all powers on themselves, including the power to force-unmute a participant. The privacy issue is easily solved by enforcing the presence of an overlay stating that \"during this call, the moderator has the power to do so and so\" when a participant joins the meeting, and by applying some visual indicator that the user has been unmuted.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
